{
  "schemaVersion": "akm.eval.config.v1",
  "run": {
    "id": "memory-comparison-smoke",
    "outputDir": "runs/memory-comparison-smoke",
    "maxConcurrency": 1,
    "timeoutMs": 1800000
  },
  "packs": [
    {
      "id": "longmemeval-smoke",
      "adapter": "longmemeval",
      "enabled": true,
      "config": {
        "evaluatorCommand": "python scripts/longmemeval-evaluator.py",
        "evaluatorModel": "gpt-4o",
        "maxQuestions": 100,
        "questionCategories": [
          "single-session",
          "multi-session",
          "temporal",
          "preference"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variants": [
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "agent": {
        "provider": "openai-compatible",
        "providerRef": "openai-compatible",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini"
      },
      "akm": {
        "enabled": false
      },
      "memory": {
        "backend": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "akm-memory",
      "agent": {
        "provider": "openai-compatible",
        "providerRef": "openai-compatible",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini"
      },
      "akm": {
        "enabled": true,
        "command": "akm"
      },
      "memory": {
        "backend": "akm"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "raw-vector",
      "agent": {
        "provider": "openai-compatible",
        "providerRef": "openai-compatible",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini"
      },
      "akm": {
        "enabled": false
      },
      "memory": {
        "backend": "raw-vector"
      }
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "baseline, raw-vector, and akm-memory are truthful runnable benchmark choices; the akm arm shells out to a real akm CLI (see docs/memory-backends.md) and needs one reachable via AKM_EVAL_AKM_CMD (default [\"akm\"]).",
    "Competitor backends (mem0, Zep, OpenViking) were removed from this repo: a competitor arm we configure ourselves is a strawman risk under docs/comparability.md A8. Cross-tool comparison is done by running the vendor's own published tool, or by citing their published benchmark figures, once our own numbers are Tier-A compliant."
  ],
  "providers": {
    "openai-compatible": {
      "type": "openai-compatible",
      "baseURL": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
      "apiKey": "{env:OPENAI_API_KEY}",
      "defaultModel": "gpt-4o-mini"
    }
  },
  "judging": {
    "enabled": true,
    "provider": "openai",
    "model": "gpt-4.1-mini",
    "temperature": 0
  },
  "telemetry": {
    "trackTokens": true,
    "trackCost": true,
    "trackLatency": true,
    "captureLogs": true
  }
}
